 ok←test_flattened(folder name);main;dup;opts;ns;goo;goofile;dupfile;foo;foofile;z;_;Layout;layouts;expected;fastLoad;i
     ⍝ Test the flattened scenario

 FLAT_TARGET←'app' ⍝ simulated user input to onFlatWrite: declare target folder for new function

 {}3 QMKDIR Retry⊢folder
 {}3 QMKDIR folder,'/app'
 {}3 QMKDIR folder,'/utils'

      ⍝ ↓↓↓ Do not use QNPUT for these, they must NOT be asynchonous
 _←(⊂main←' r←main' 'r←dup 2')⎕NPUT folder,'/app/main.aplf'        ⍝ One "application" function
 _←(⊂dup←' r←dup x' 'r←x x')⎕NPUT dupfile←folder,'/utils/dup.aplf' ⍝ One "utility" function

 opts←⎕NS''
 opts.(flatten source)←1 'dir'
 opts.getFilename←TESTNS,'.onFlatFilename'
 z←opts LinkCreate name folder

 ns←#⍎name

 assert'''dup'' ''main'' ≡ ns.⎕NL ¯3'           ⍝ Validate both fns are in root namespace
 assert'2 2≡ns.main'                            ⍝ Check that main function works

 dup,←⊂' ⍝ Modified dup'
 ns'dup'⎕SE.Link.Fix dup                        ⍝ Redefine existing function dup
 assert'dup≡⊃⎕NGET dupfile 1'
 assert'dupfile≡4⊃5179⌶''ns.dup'''             ⍝   ... await callback & link established

 goofile←folder,'/app/goo.aplf'

 ns'goo'⎕SE.Link.Fix↑goo←' r←goo x' ' r←x x x'  ⍝ Add a new function, this time using a matrix
 assert'goo≡⊃⎕NGET goofile 1'
 assert'goofile≡4⊃5179⌶''ns.goo'''             ⍝   ... await callback & link established

 ns'foo' 'goo'⎕SE.Link.Fix foo←' r←foo x' ' r←x x x' ⍝ Simulate RENAME of existing foo > goo

 foofile←∊((⊂'foo')@2)⎕NPARTS goofile           ⍝ Expected name of the new file
 assert'foo≡⊃⎕NGET foofile 1'                   ⍝ Validate file has the right contents
 assert'foofile≡4⊃5179⌶''ns.foo'''             ⍝   ... and foo is linked to the right file

 Breathe ⍝ Allow backlog of FSW events to clear on slow machines
 _←QNDELETE foofile
 assert'''dup'' ''goo'' ''main''≡ns.⎕nl -3' '⎕EX ''ns.foo'''
      ⍝ link issue #781: when flattening, directories define no APL name and must not clash with same-named files
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break name ⋄ ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder
 Layout←{ ⍝ create files in folder from relative paths - a function or scripted namespace named after each file
     _←3 ⎕MKDIR folder
     {(dir base ext)←⎕NPARTS folder,'/',⍵
         _←3 ⎕MKDIR dir
         src←((' r←',base)'r←1')((':Namespace ',base)':EndNamespace')⊃⍨1+ext≡'.apln'
         (⊂src)⎕NPUT(folder,'/',⍵)1
     }¨⍵
 }
 layouts←('FOO.aplf' 'FOO/code.aplf')('FOO/FOO.aplf' 'bar.aplf')('util.apln' 'util/x.aplf')
 expected←('FOO' 'code')('FOO' 'bar')('util'(,'x'))
 :For fastLoad :In 0 1
     opts←⎕NS'' ⋄ opts.(source flatten fastLoad)←'dir' 1 fastLoad
     :For i :In ⍳≢layouts                                ⍝ A, B and C link, with flattened names
         Layout i⊃layouts
         z←opts LinkCreate name folder
         'link issue #781'assert'~∨/''ERRORS ENCOUNTERED''⍷z'
         z←(⍎name).⎕NL-3 9
         'link issue #781'assert'(i⊃expected)≡z[⍋↑z]'
         {}⎕SE.Link.Break name ⋄ ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder
     :EndFor
     opts.flatten←0                                       ⍝ without flatten, B links: FOO is a namespace containing a function FOO
     Layout 2⊃layouts
     z←opts LinkCreate name folder
     'link issue #781'assert'~∨/''ERRORS ENCOUNTERED''⍷z'
     'link issue #781'assert'9.1 3.1≡',name,'.⎕NC''FOO'' ''bar'''
     'link issue #781'assert'3=',name,'.FOO.⎕NC''FOO'''
     {}⎕SE.Link.Break name ⋄ ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder
 :EndFor
      ⍝ genuine clashes are still detected (fastLoad does not detect clashes and fails later, leaving fixed items behind - not tested here)
 opts.(flatten fastLoad)←1 0
 Layout'a/Foo.aplf' 'b/Foo.aplf'                         ⍝ two files defining the same flattened name
 'link issue #781'assertError'opts LinkCreate name folder' 'clashing APL names'
 assert'{6::1 ⋄ 0=CountLinks}⍬'
 ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder
 opts.flatten←0                                           ⍝ without flatten, A and C clash
 :For i :In 1 3
     Layout i⊃layouts
     'link issue #781'assertError'opts LinkCreate name folder' 'clashing APL names'
     assert'{6::1 ⋄ 0=CountLinks}⍬'
     ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder
 :EndFor

      ⍝ link issue #782: Diff and Resync must match items to files in a flattened link, so Break → Create can relink an unchanged namespace
 opts←⎕NS'' ⋄ opts.(source flatten)←'dir' 1
 :For layouts :In ('Foo.aplf' 'Goo.aplf')('Foo.aplf' 'sub/Goo.aplf')  ⍝ root-only and nested layouts
     Layout layouts
     z←opts LinkCreate name folder
     'link issue #782'assert'0∊⍴⎕SE.Link.Diff name'                              ⍝ nothing changed: no differences
     'link issue #782'assert'1∊''No action required''⍷⎕SE.Link.Resync name'
     {}⎕SE.Link.Break name
     z←opts LinkCreate name folder                                                ⍝ relink unchanged namespace (link issue #230)
     'link issue #782'assert'~∨/''ERRORS ENCOUNTERED''⍷z'
     'link issue #782'assert'0∊⍴⎕SE.Link.Diff name'
     _←(⊂' r←Goo' 'r←782')⎕NPUT(folder,'/',⊃⌽layouts)1                            ⍝ change one file
     'link issue #782'assert'1=≢⎕SE.Link.Diff name'                              ⍝ exactly one difference
     {}⎕SE.Link.Break name
     _←(⊂' r←Goo' 'r←1')⎕NPUT(folder,'/',⊃⌽layouts)1                              ⍝ restore the file, but modify the workspace item after Break
     _←(⍎name).⎕FX' r←Goo' 'r←783'
     _←(⍎name).⎕FX' r←Extra' 'r←788'                                              ⍝ and add an item that no file defines
     opts.source←'auto'
     'link issue #782'assertError'opts LinkCreate name folder' 'non-empty namespace' ⍝ a modified item must still prevent relinking with source=auto
     opts.source←'dir'
     z←opts LinkCreate name folder                                                ⍝ link issue #788: explicit source=dir replaces Goo from its file and leaves Extra alone
     'link issue #788'assert'~∨/''ERRORS ENCOUNTERED''⍷z'
     'link issue #788'assert'1=(⍎name).Goo'
     'link issue #788'assert'788=(⍎name).Extra'
     'link issue #788'assert'(,⊂''→'' ''',name,'.Extra'')≡↓2↑⍤1⊢⎕SE.Link.Diff name' ⍝ the only difference is the extra item
     {}⎕SE.Link.Break name ⋄ ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder
 :EndFor
      ⍝ link issue #782: forceFilenames must work when flattening (the file names are computed by the same code as Diff uses)
 Layout,⊂'Foo.aplf'
 _←(⊂' r←Goo' 'r←2')⎕NPUT(folder,'/sub/goo.aplf')1⊣3 ⎕MKDIR folder,'/sub'         ⍝ wrong case: must be renamed to Goo.aplf
 opts.forceFilenames←1
 z←opts LinkCreate name folder
 'link issue #782'assert'~∨/''ERRORS ENCOUNTERED''⍷z'
 'link issue #782'assert'⎕NEXISTS folder,''/sub/Goo.aplf'''
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break name ⋄ ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder
      ⍝ link issue #789: items must be tied under watch=ns, so that an edit of a flattened item is written to its own file rather than to the link root
 opts←⎕NS'' ⋄ opts.(source flatten watch)←'dir' 1 'ns'
 3 ⎕MKDIR¨(folder,'/')∘,¨'app' 'utils'
 _←(⊂' r←app' 'r←42')⎕NPUT(folder,'/app/code.aplf')1
 _←(⊂' r←utils' 'r←1')⎕NPUT(folder,'/utils/code.aplf')1
 z←opts LinkCreate name folder
 'link issue #789'assert'(folder,''/app/code.aplf'')≡4⊃',name,'.(5179⌶)''app'''
 (⍎name)'app'⎕SE.Link.Fix' r←app' 'r←789'
 'link issue #789'assert'('' r←app'' ''r←789'')≡⊃⎕NGET(folder,''/app/code.aplf'')1'
 'link issue #789'assert'~⎕NEXISTS folder,''/app.aplf'''
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break name ⋄ ⎕EX name ⋄ 3 ⎕NDELETE folder

 CleanUp folder name
 ok←1
